# Names only. Hosted-database tooling (never the production project). Put real values in database/.env.live (git-ignored).
# RIO_DEV_PROJECT_REF=               20-character ref of the DEV project; scripts/db-dev.ts refuses the .env project
# RIO_CONFIRM_PROVISION=            set to the dev ref ONLY for one `npm run staff:provision` command (needs RIO_LIVE_CONFIRM too)
# RIO_STAFF_PASSWORD=                optional, for ONE non-interactive provisioning command only; never put it in a file. The script otherwise asks at a hidden prompt
# RIO_CONFIRM_PUSH=                  set to the dev ref only when you really intend `npm run db:dev:push`
# RIO_LIVE_URL=                      dev project URL (or http://127.0.0.1:54321 for a local stack)
# RIO_LIVE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# RIO_LIVE_SECRET_KEY=               server-side test setup only; bypasses RLS
# RIO_LIVE_CONFIRM=                  set to the dev ref to allow `npm run test:live` to write test rows
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=              read by the Supabase CLI for the dev database
#
# IPv4 Session Pooler URL for the DEV project (dashboard > Connect > Session pooler; port 5432 only).
# Contains the database password: keep it only in .env.live and never paste it into chat or logs.
# SUPABASE_DEV_POOLER_URL=postgresql://postgres.<dev ref>:<password>@aws-N-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
#
